**How to Apply These Commits Locally**

If you are setting up the repository from scratch, you can run these commands sequentially in your terminal:

```bash
# 1. Initialize and commit repository structure
git init
git add LICENSE .gitignore
git commit -m "chore: initialize repository structure and configuration"

# 2. Add GushClient core code
git add src/GushClient.php
git commit -m "feat: implement core GushClient class"

# 3. Add public proxy endpoint
git add public/index.php public/chat
git commit -m "feat: build secure server-side chat proxy endpoint"

# 4. Add security features
git add src/RateLimiter.php src/CorsHandler.php
git commit -m "feat: add CORS protection and file-backed rate limiting"

# 5. Add documentation
git add README.md
git commit -m "docs: add comprehensive README and deployment guide"
```

